WEBVTT

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.330
Come in.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.080
Good morning, Jun.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.080
Breakfast is ready.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.800
Good morning, Kaya-san.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.770
It seems a bit bland.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.220
Yes, you're right.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.250
Bring over the salt, would you?

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.760
Muscle Salt

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.040
Are you making fun of us?

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.860
This isn't who I am!

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.860
Today's another scorcher, huh?

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.890
Hajime-chan!

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.510
Come on, it's morning, Hajime-chan!

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.540
You'll be late, Hajime-chan.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.280
Kaya's gonna yell if you're late.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.130
Morning, Arashi-san.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.640
Morning, Hajime-chan.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.600
What were you doing? Were you up all night?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.820
Yeah.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.440
Science Made Fun

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:10.730
In our time, there's this annoying thing called "Free Study" that's part of our homework.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.570
Experimental Science Guidebook

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.150
What do you think this is?

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.090
Just looks like a cherry.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.790
It is a masterpiece created by me, Yasaka Hajime!

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.930
And I call it...

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.440
THE CHERRY BOMB!

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.180
Cherry bomb?

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.790
At first glance, it just looks like an ordinary cherry...

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.240
HOWEVER!

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.390
In reality...

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:37.970
Inside is a mix of pop rocks, Cayenne, Japanese, and normal pepper,

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:41.030
along with powdered wasabi!

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:46.570
Playback Part I
Master

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:50.110
Anyway, I don't think "bomb" is really a good idea.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.490
Then what should I do?

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:54.760
Change the name.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.600
Call it "Cutie Cherry-chan," maybe?

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.510
I'm turning this in at school!

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.300
I can't name it something like that!

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.620
But it's cute!

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.710
The matter's settled. Cutie Cherry-chan it is!

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.680
Come on...

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.720
Man, this Cutie Cherry I made is the ultimate weapon.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.210
It's perfect.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.060
I can't wait to see it in action.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.750
What are you smirking about, Yasaka?

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.310
Nothing!

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:28.690
I guess if I had to say, it would be a mad scientist's crazed laughter.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.780
Huh?

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.130
Oh, right. Something was bugging me.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.340
What is it, Master?

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.680
Actually...

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.730
It's Akagi Keiichiro!

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.530
Excuse me.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.590
She really likes him.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.960
Actually, so do I.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.230
I wonder if it's really him.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.640
I guess I'll go see, too.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.230
Me, too.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.230
You're going too?

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:59.560
What, you don't understand the attraction of the third man, Tony?

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.820
I'll show you.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.610
Come with me.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.460
Wait, Tony-

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.450
No one's here.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.620
Maybe it was a prank?

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:14.070
Come to think of it, Akagi Keiichiro died before I was born.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.690
Remember that in the first place!

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.940
Jeez, what a waste of time...

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.180
I think it's in a slightly different place.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.170
So, what were you talking about?

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.430
Actually, this here, you see...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.900
Again?

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:35.480
There was one more in the back of the fridge.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.970
What is that?

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.120
Expired milk.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.330
June 1st...

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:42.790
That was two months ago.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:46.230
I want you to time travel back to May with this.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:51.350
Oh, that makes sense. If it hasn't expired yet, you can drink it!

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.770
That does <i>not</i> make sense!

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.400
Is it not OK?

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:58.250
Spoiled milk is spoiled, no matter where you take it.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:02.200
It's the same reason you don't get younger when you go to the past.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.670
You won't be able to drink it.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.130
Oh, I get it!

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:11.150
Arashi-san, is it possible you're just now realizing this?

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:14.910
Master, stop trying to fool people.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.530
Someone might really believe you.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:21.730
Come on. After last time, I contemplated it and came up with a better way.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.350
The problem is we're trying to drink the expired milk.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.490
Go back in time, to before it expires, and trade it for the one that hasn't expired yet.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:34.090
Then bring the fresh milk back to the present and drink it?

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.310
I see.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.960
That would work.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.660
Since it's just sitting in the fridge and no one drank it,

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:44.880
there's no problem with exchanging it for the spoiled milk.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.620
Wow, you're smart, Master!

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.000
I don't really get it, but nice one!

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:58.950
Naw... Anyway, go back to the past and trade this for a fresh one.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.890
This still doesn't seem right.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:04.070
If it sounds like a good idea to Master, that's good enough for me.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.110
Huh?

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:08.050
What's wrong, Jun?

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:10.890
If we take this to the past and it works-

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:14.370
no, let's say it already did work-

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:19.870
that would mean this milk spoiled once and we took it to the past. And then it spoiled again,

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:23.070
Past

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:23.070
June 1st

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:23.070
Today

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:23.070
Future

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:23.090
so it's spoiled twice, right?

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.270
Twice

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:28.180
That implies it's already repeated those two months twice.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:34.630
Therefore, it's four months expired!

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.640
Who cares?

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.850
No one's drinking it, so who cares if it's been spoiled for two or four months?

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.080
That's true...

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:44.550
Wait!

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:50.510
Doesn't that mean there should be two old milks in the refrigerator?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:58.030
Past

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:58.030
June 1st

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:58.030
Today

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:58.030
Future

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:54.900
If it's gone through these past two months twice, then both the two-month-old milk

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.430
Four Months

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:55.760
Two Months

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.060
and the four-month-old milk should be in the fridge.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.430
Two Cartons

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.750
But there was only this one.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:08.390
I know what happens. Effects on a quantum level suddenly cause it to spoil twice as much!

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:14.000
Like Schrödinger's cat-opening and observing inside the carton causes the quantum wave function

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.990
to collapse, becoming milk four months past its expiration date!

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.250
Collapse

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:19.940
The uncertainty principle, right?

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.770
You know some complicated things, huh?

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:27.100
It was in a book the detective brought me.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.760
No, wait!

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.440
That doesn't make sense.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:34.190
We go back, return with unspoiled milk, and drink it. Right?

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:41.320
Past

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:41.320
June 1st

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:41.320
Today

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:41.320
Future

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.380
Time Travel

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:34.710
Glug

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:35.320
That's right.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:35.810
Glug

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:38.600
If we drink it, the milk vanishes while it's still fresh.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:36.970
Glug

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.640
Disappear

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.640
Disappear

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:41.330
Thus, the expired milk, itself, ceases to exist!

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:40.930
Impossible

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.250
So there shouldn't be any milk left!

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.600
The more that we drink before it's spoiled,

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.220
the more of the milk will spoil, no?

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:55.520
We've proven that time travel can't change history.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:00.240
The simultaneous existence of spoiled milk and unspoiled, drunk milk is impossible.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.430
Does drinkable milk actually exist?

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.480
Which milk spoils?

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:16.040
We may be staring in the face of an incredible time paradox, previously unsolved.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:21.790
This is a mystery never before seen by humanity!

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:25.640
I'm going to go buy some new milk.
Let's throw this out.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:32.030
Humanity's mystery!

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:36.710
Welcome!

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:38.640
Hey, Arashi-san.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.120
Yamashiro-san.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:45.660
It's hot today, Arashi-san.
Aren't you warm in that kimono?

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.580
I'm fine. Actually, I get a lot of fresh air.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.210
The jerk...

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:57.390
He forgot he owes us for saving him,
and now he's going after Arashi-san.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:59.890
Ungrateful bastard!

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:02.970
But I've got just the thing for you.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:06.120
You always order a lemon squash.

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:12.880
I'll put my new weapon, Cutie Cherry-chan, in your lemon squash, and that'll show you!

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.760
Taste my ultimate weapon.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.250
Have you decided on your order?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:22.580
Let's see... I'll have my usual strawberry shortcake and some green tea.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:23.800
OK!

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.010
Why?

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:29.980
Not your usual lemon squash?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:33.570
Sometimes, it's nice to have a hot drink on a hot day.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.950
It makes you sweat and cools you down, doesn't it?

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:38.700
Oh, no!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.200
I never calculated for the possibility that he would change his drink!

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.550
Is this plan a failure?

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:44.350
No, I still have some more tricks up my sleeve!

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.410
What are you doing, Yasaka?

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.170
Cherries don't go in the green tea.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.680
I'm just adding special service for a regular.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.550
That's not "special service." That's being a dick.

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:06.750
It doesn't matter, as long as I add sincerity!

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.010
It does so!

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.210
Oh, my. You done?

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.250
I'll take this.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.940
A-Arashi-san...

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.780
Here you are.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:18.850
I worked on it all night, too.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.400
That sounds interesting!

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.420
I'll bring the book next time.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.750
Really?

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.630
I can't wait!

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:38.270
Jeez, if I'd known this would happen,
I'd have put it in the cake, not the drink...

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.990
I bought some new milk.

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:45.160
What? Is this the expensive stuff?

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:49.350
It's organic milk, from cows raised on chemical-free natural feed.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.270
This time, drink it before it expires.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:56.010
Oh, and cherries were on sale, so I bought a bunch.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.620
Oh... Maybe I'll make a free menu from them.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.270
Cherry Day

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:12.320
Here are your free cherries.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.260
Here you are.

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:17.060
Enjoy some cherries, too.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:19.330
Here you go. Something special for you, Yamashiro-san.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:21.690
Thank you, Arashi-san.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.210
I should've just done that from the start!

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.220
These are good.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.870
You try one too.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:30.710
I'm fine.

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:32.890
Come on.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.120
I don't want it!

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.700
I don't even want to look at cherries!

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:43.250
What's your problem?

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.400
Weird kid...

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:53.110
Is this the Cutie Cherry-chan?

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.860
This is Hajime-chan's.
Do not eat!!

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:58.080
It'd be really bad if you accidentally gave it to a customer. I'll hold on to it.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.750
Ah, Arashi-san, that's a normal cherry...

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:07.150
No, more importantly, the
Cutie Cherry-chan is in there.

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:10.750
Oh, give me one.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.390
These are good.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.390
I'll take one, too, I guess.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.390
May I have one, also?

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.160
Me, too.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.530
My, these are good.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:31.540
They're juicy and sweet!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.170
This is Russian roulette.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:39.120
I need to do something or I'll go nuts!

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.630
Oh, right, Arashi-san. Can you do this?

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:46.460
Wow!

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:47.820
I'll try it, too.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:48.860
Me, too.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.280
May I try it as well?

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.960
What are you doing?!

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:55.980
Huh? Is something wrong?

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:57.930
See?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.140
Master's pretty good, isn't she?

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.910
Did you know?

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:06.520
People who can do this are good at kissing.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:08.700
K-K-Kis-

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:13.890
What are you teaching Yayoi?!

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.530
What? I didn't do any-

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:21.330
Good, no one got it.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:23.430
Think logically.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:26.250
Somewhere in there is the Cutie Cherry-chan.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:30.160
My ultimate goal is to recover or destroy it before it hits someone.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:35.510
Or, if possible, to target Yamashiro with it, per my original objective.

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:40.180
For that to happen, I must be able to determine the original Cutie Cherry-chan.

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:44.260
But my work was perfect, so I can't tell them apart.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.920
Super Awesome

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.920
Unparalleled

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:47.640
There are three possible options here.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.710
One: Recover them all.

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:53.700
Two: Destroy them all.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:58.120
Three: Feed them all to Yamashiro.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.750
What? I can't eat all these.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:06.710
They say people can eat as many cherries as they want, so eat up!

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.800
What are you doing?

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:13.450
Something special for a regular customer...

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.860
That's not "special." It's being a dick.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.330
There's such a thing as a limit.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:22.060
That won't work, huh?

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.100
I know!

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:26.630
The problem is that I try to deal with it once it's in there.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:37.470
Past

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:37.470
Morning

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:30.930
Everything's fine if a real cherry gets thrown in.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:36.270
I'll just time travel to the past and replace the Cutie Cherry-chan with a real cherry!

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.300
Time Travel

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.760
Removed

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:40.340
But that means I need to take a real cherry back to the past.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.560
Real

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:43.640
If I screw up and take the Cutie Cherry-chan instead...

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:42.520
Cutie Cherry

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:45.630
I know!

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.580
Kitchen

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:47.580
Go back to this morning?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:53.870
Yes, I want to take the Cutie Cherry-chan that you took from me back to this morning.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:58.430
I was thinking about what the master said about the milk this morning...

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:03.000
Oh, taking something spoiled into the past and exchanging it, right?

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.200
I thought we'd do an experiment with the Cutie Cherry-chan.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.040
Experiment?

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:08.970
For my free study.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:10.240
Free study!

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.520
For my homework...

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:14.900
It was a real cherry she took.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.230
This is Hajime-chan's.
Do not eat!!

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:18.780
If I take it back to the past and exchange it, we're all good.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:21.660
I see. If it's for homework, it can't be helped.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.880
Wait a second. I'll go get it.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:33.200
How many times do we have to tell Master before she understands?

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.250
Just drink it before it spoils...

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.730
I spent all that money on organic milk, too.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:39.770
Let's exchange it and go home.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.110
Jun, please run the decoy plan.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:44.230
I guess I have to.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.200
Hajime-chan's.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.020
OK, Hajime-chan.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:50.440
Ah! It's Kobayashi Akira!

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:50.430
Hajime-chan's.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.400
Excuse me.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.380
She really likes him.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:56.210
Actually, so do I.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:17:00.160
I'll show you the attraction of Might Guy.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.260
Everybody went outside.

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:06.700
Well done, Jun.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.000
Let's exchange the milk right away.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.430
We did this before, didn't we?

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:14.720
I'm pretty sure I yelled, "It's Takakura Ken!"

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:17.040
Takakura Ken?

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:19.960
I remember now.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:24.870
When that happened, I received unbelievable humiliation at the hands of Hajime.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.700
I won't forget it until the day I die!

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.020
You're already a ghost.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:37.490
All right. I'll show Hajime just what he did!

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:42.430
I'll mix wasabi powder and Japanese pepper with cayenne and normal pepper,

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.550
then add Tabasco to make a super-spicy cream!

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:48.980
Then I'll cut a cherry in half and scoop out the insides with a spoon,

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.800
then put that cream inside, and seal it!

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:53.290
And then...

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:57.330
Put it together with cellophane tape, and it's done.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:58.830
Cellophane tape?

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:02.010
Don't worry. It's transparent, so he won't see it.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:07.740
This tiny difference in common knowledge reminds me that she's from the past.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.430
See? You can't tell.

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:13.520
Amazing! Her skill has overcome the inherent flaws in the technology.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:18.410
I'll make him eat this and understand the humiliation I suffered.

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:19.690
Hajime-chan's

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:25.240
Um, Kaya-san. Is that the, um...

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:27.910
No way.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:31.790
I thought for sure that was because of Master's arm.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.920
Have I made something awful?

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:38.300
Ah! I'm disappearing!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:41.180
Might Guy wasn't there.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.200
Too bad. Maybe he was busy filming.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:46.450
Oh, no. We have to go!

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:47.440
Wait, Jun!

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:49.190
If we don't act, something terrible happens.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.510
It's too late, Kaya-san!

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:51.360
There's no time left.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:52.050
We'll disappear!

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.570
No, no!

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.430
Is it impossible to change history?

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.060
You sure it wasn't a trick?

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:05.340
I was hoping that Might Guy would fulfill my hopes...

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:06.740
What's with the self-confidence?

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:11.300
If you leave this out, it'll spoil.

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:14.570
I'd better put it where we can see it, so it won't spoil.

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:20.020
OK, Hajime-chan. Let's go.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.500
Right.

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:35.940
Now then, the only question is how to switch this with the Cutie Cherry-chan.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.230
We're inside the café...

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:40.360
Leave that to me.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:44.370
It's Akagi Keiichiro!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.770
Ah... This morning, that was you...

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:02.070
I'm exhausted.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.950
It was really busy today.

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:06.940
It was thanks to the cherries Kaya-san bought.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:08.600
We used almost all of them.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:15.990
The cherries are one thing, but please drink the milk before it spoils, Master.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:18.430
True that.

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:21.220
All right! As a reward, I'll make you some fruit juice.

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:22.550
What?

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.580
OK, I took out the detonator.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.260
It won't explode now.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.320
Ah... That was close.

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:34.130
I need to learn my lesson from this

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:37.590
and next time, design something that takes them out in one hit.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.260
So, how was your free study?

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.150
Huh?

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:44.440
What happened when you took it to the past and switched it?

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:47.370
It went perfect!

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:48.220
Perfect!

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:52.020
Here you go.

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.270
Drink up!

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:06.960
That's Kaya and the rest screaming.

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:08.940
Maybe they saw Might Guy.

00:22:42.990 --> 00:22:45.750
So, I read a fascinating book yesterday.

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:48.830
Yeah, what was it called?

00:22:48.830 --> 00:22:52.590
Well... I forgot the title.

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:55.550
Tell me what kind of story it was.

00:22:55.550 --> 00:22:57.530
Sure, why not.

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:02.750
It was the story of a boy, much troubled by justice.

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:09.230
He worships a legendary hero and, in his zeal to fight evil and wield the hammer of justice,

00:23:09.230 --> 00:23:11.540
he hurts those who are innocent.

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:18.290
With his brilliant mind, he fights a pitched psychological battle with a detective,

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:21.390
but troubled by his crimes, he...

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:25.420
That's <i>Crime and Punishment.</i>

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:28.880
<i>Dostoevsky?</i>

00:23:29.930 --> 00:23:35.180
Illustration by Jin Kobayashi
